hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5941","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar And Abdullah bin Ubaid said: The verse combined Ubadah bin al-Samit and Muawiyah. Ubadah told them, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, about selling gold for gold, paper for paper, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and dates for dates One of them: And salt for salt, and the other did not say it, except like for like, hand to hand, and he commanded us to sell gold for paper, and paper With gold, and wheat with barley, and barley with wheat, hand in hand, as we wish. One of them said: So whoever increases or increases, has made arbiy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5942","Al-Mu'mal bin Hisham told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Alqama, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Muslim bin Yasar told me And Abdullah bin Ubaid, who was called Ibn Hurmuz, said: The matter combined the matter between Ubadah bin al-Samit and Muawiyah, so Ubadah rose up He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for dates, and wheat for wheat. And barley for barley. One of them said: And salt for salt, and the other did not say it, except equal for equal, like for like. One of them said: Who He increased, or increased, then he increased, and the other did not say, and we were commanded to sell gold for silver, silver for gold, and wheat for barley. “And barley for wheat, hand in hand, as we like.”"
"5943","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Salamah bin Alqamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: he told me Muslim bin Yassar and Abdullah bin Ubaid said: The matter combined the matter between Ubadah bin al-Samit and Muawiyah, so Ubadah said: “The Messenger of God forbade God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said that we sell gold for gold, paper for paper, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and dates for dates. So one of them said: And salt for salt, and the other did not say, except like for like, like for like. One of them said: who increased or increased, So he raised interest, and the other did not say so, and he commanded us to sell gold for silver, paper for gold, wheat for barley, and barley for wheat. Hand in hand, as we like.” Then the hadith reached Muawiyah, so he stood up and said: What is the matter with men who narrate hadiths on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? We accompanied him, but we did not hear it from him! This reached the level of worship, so he stood up, repeated the hadith, and said: Let us narrate what we heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, even though Muawiya. Qatada disagreed with him and narrated it on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Ubadah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5944","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muslim ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, On the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who was Badr, and he pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so as not to fear, for God’s sake, the blame of the blamer. Ubadah ibn al-Samit stood up as a preacher and said: “O people, you have initiated trades that I do not know what they are!! By weight, its weight and its kind, and silver is for silver, weight for weight, its weight and its kind, and there is no harm in selling silver for gold outright. In one hand, most of them are silver, and they are not good for bad. Indeed, wheat is for wheat, and barley is for barley, one ebb for another, and there is no harm in selling barley. With wheat, hand to hand, and barley, most of them, and is not suitable for a bad one. Indeed, dates for dates, one tide to another, until he mentioned salt, one tide to another. So whoever increases, or increases, has committed arbi.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5945","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, saying: Amr bin Asim told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatada told us. On the authority of Abu al-Khalil, on the authority of Muslim al-Makki, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Gold for gold, its ground and its kind, weight for weight, and silver for silver, its ground and its kind, weight for weight, and salt For salt, and dates for dates, and wheat for wheat, and barley for barley, measure for measure. So whoever increases or increases has raised, and there is no harm in selling. \Barley for wheat"
"5946","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Khalid, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us He said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Selling gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt, except... Like for like, the same for the same, so whoever does more or more has committed arbi.” The word is for Muhammad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5947","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Ali, that Abu Al-Mutawakkil passed by them in the market, so he stood up to him A people I am among. He said: We said: We have come to you to ask you about morphology. He said: I heard Abu Sa`id al-Khudri. A man said to him: What is between you and the Prophet? Is there anyone other than Abu Saeed, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: There is no one but him between me and him. He said: He said: “Gold for gold, and paper for paper.” Solomon said: Or he said: Silver for silver. And wheat for wheat, and barley for barley, and dates for dates, and salt for salt, all the same for the same, so whoever adds to that, or adds more, He has shown interest, and the taker and the giver are alike in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5948","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Hakim bin Jabir told us, on the authority of Ubadah bin al-Samit, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Gold is one size for another, and silver is one level for another,” until he specified: “Salt is a hand with a hand.” Muawiyah said: This does not say anything. Ubadah said: By God, I do not care if I am not in a land where there is Muawiyah, I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say that. The pronunciation is for Aaron"
"5949","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Tamim, on the authority of Saeed bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A dinar for a dinar, and a dirham for a dirham, there is no preference between them.”"
"5950","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Humaid bin Qays al-Makki, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Omar said: “A dinar for a dinar, A dirham for a dirham, there is no difference between them. This is the covenant of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5951","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala Kufi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Gold for gold, weight for weight, like for like, and silver for silver, weight for weight.” “Like for like, so whoever does more or more has committed arbi.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5952","Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No You shall not sell gold for gold, except like for like, and do not exchange them one for the other, and do not sell paper for paper, except like for like, and do not Share some of them in exchange for others, and do not sell any of them for something that is absent or something that is incomplete.”"
"5953","Humayd bin Masada and Ismail bin Saud told us, saying: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Ibn Awn told us, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: My eyes saw and my ears heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he mentioned “the prohibition of gold.” “For gold, and paper for paper, except like for like, and like for like, and do not sell something that is absent for something that is complete, and do not exchange one of them over the other.”"
"5954","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, that Mu’awiyah “sold a gold siqab.” Or paper, with more than its weight. Abu Darda’ said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding something like this, except \like for like\"""""
"5955","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Shuja’ Saeed bin Yazid, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, on the authority of Hanash Al-San’ani, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, said: On the day of Khaybar, I bought a necklace that had gold and beads in it. I took it apart and found in it more than Twelve dinars, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said, “It should not be sold until it is detailed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5956","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Muhammad bin Mahboub told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, on the authority of Hanash al-Sana’ani, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid al-Ansari, who said: On the Day of Khaybar, I found a necklace containing gold and beads. So I wanted to sell them, so I mentioned, meaning, to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Separate some of them from others, then sell them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5957","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, who said: A partner of mine sold a paper for a small amount, so he came to me. So he told me, and I said: This is not appropriate, and he said: By God, I sold it in the market, and no one criticized me, so I went to Al-Baraa bin Aazib. So I asked him, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us in Medina, and we were doing this sale, and he said: “As long as it was hand to hand, there is no problem with it.” “And as long as he is not a shareholder, he is usury.” Then he said to me: “Come to Zayd ibn Arqam.” So I went to him and asked him, and he said something like that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5958","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Amr bin Dinar and Aamir bin Musab told me, They heard Abu Al-Minhal say: I asked Al-Baraa bin Azib and Zayd bin Arqam, and they said: We were merchants at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, so we asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about exchange, and he said: “If it is hand to hand, then there is no problem, and if it is bad, then there is no problem.” \fits\"""""
"5959","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Habib, he said: I heard Abu Al-Minhal, he said : I asked Al-Baraa about the morphology, and he said: Ask Zaid bin Arqam; He is better than me and more knowledgeable, so they all said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade paper and gold as a religion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5960","And while Ahmad bin Mani’ was read to us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Ishaq told us, he said: He told us Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us from selling silver for silver, and gold.” “For gold, unless they are equal, and He commanded us to buy gold for silver, however we wish, and silver for gold, however we wish.”"
"5961","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salam told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from selling Silver for silver, except an eye for an eye, equal for an equal, and we do not sell gold for gold, except an eye for an eye, and equal for an equal, and the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Trade gold for silver as you wish, and silver for gold as you wish. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: News of Abu Tawbah came between Yahya bin Abi Kathir and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra: Yahya bin Abi Ishaq (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5962","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid, that he heard Ibn Abbas, saying: Usama told me Ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “usury, except in the case of an unpaid one.”"
"5963","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Salih, he heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri say: I told Ibn Abbas: Did you see what you said, something you found in the Book of God, or something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I did not find it in the Book of God, nor did I hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but Usama bin Zaid told me that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Usury is only in the interest.”"
"5964","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that Ibn Abbas, he said: Osama told me Ibn Zayd, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “There is no usury except in the case of an unpaid debt.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5965","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell Gold for silver, and silver for gold, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him about that, and he said: “If you pledge allegiance Your companion, do not separate from him while there is confusion between you and him.”"
"5966","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: Muammal informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar “He saw no harm in extracting dirhams from dinars, and dinars from dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5967","Ahmad bin Yahya told me, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: I was selling camels in Al-Baqi’, selling for dinars and taking dirhams, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the house of Hafsa. So I said: O Messenger of God, I want to ask you: I sell for Baqi’, so I sell for dinars, and I take dirhams. He said: “There is no harm in You take it at its current price, as long as nothing separates you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5968","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told us, he said: Al-Mu’affa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Slowly, I ask you: I sell camels in Al-Baqi’ for dinars, and take dirhams? He said: “There is no harm in taking it at that day’s price, as long as you do not separate and there is something between you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5969","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Muharib bin Dathar told me, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “ When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Medina, he called for a scale, and it weighed for me, and added more to me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5970","Muhammad bin Mansour and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “ The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, judged me and rewarded me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5971","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais, he said: I brought Al-Abdi’s gift was a piece of fine flour from Hijr. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us while we were in Mina, and a weigher was weighed with the wages, so he bought from us. Trousers, and he said to the weigher: “Weight, and weigh.”"
"5972","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abu Safwan bin Umair said: “I sold a pair of trousers to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before the Hijra, and he gave me something in return.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: The hadith of Sufyan is more similar to authenticity than the hadith of Shu’bah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5973","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Al-Mulai, on the authority of Sufyan, H. Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abu told us Nu`aym, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hanzalah, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The measure is upon The measure of the people of Medina, and the weight is equal to the weight of the people of Mecca.” The word is for Isaac (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5974","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, according to a reading of it, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he receives it in full.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5975","Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever buys food should not sell it until he receives it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5976","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim, who is Ibn Yazid Al-Jarmi, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he has measured it.” Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with the like of it, and the one before it, “until he seizes it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5977","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “As for the one who The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it from being sold until it was fully paid, so food.”"
"5978","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: “As for the one who forbade it... Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, food is to be sold until it is seized."
"5979","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever buys food, should not sell it until he receives it.” Ibn Abbas said: I think that everything is in the same position as food. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5980","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Muhammad, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Safwan bin Mawhib, that He told him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Saifi, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not sell food Until you buy it and complete it.” Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ told me, That is on the authority of Abdullah bin Ismat Al-Jashmi, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5981","Suleiman bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Hazzam bin Hakim bin Hazzam said: 25 Hakim bin Hazzam said: I bought food as charity, and I gained from it before Take possession of it, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, and he said: “Do not sell it until you take possession of it.”"
"5982","Suleiman bin Dawud and Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us of a reading from him, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Amr bin told me Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling Someone bought food by the measure, until he fulfilled it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5983","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, said: In the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we used to buy food, and it would be sent to us. Who orders us to move it from the place where we bought it, to another place, before we sell it? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5984","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi` told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that they were They would sell food at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the top of the market indiscriminately. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade them from They sell it where it is, until they move it.”"
"5985","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us, saying: Shuaib ibn al-Layth informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar told him that they used to sell food during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Rukban, “ So he forbade them to sell it in the place where they had bought it, until they reached the food market.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5986","Nasr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: “I saw people being beaten for... “The covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that if they bought food in bulk, they would sell it until they took it to their place.”"
"5987","Muhammad ibn Adam informed me, on the authority of Hafs ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Prophet bought May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he gave him food for a certain period of time from a Jew, so he mortgaged his armor to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5988","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Anas bin Malik told us, that He walked to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with barley bread and a sacrifice of sacrifice. He said: “He pawned his armor with a Jew in Medina. So he took some barley from it for his family.”"
"5989","Amr bin Ali and Humayd bin Masada informed us, on the authority of Yazid. He said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible to advance or sell, nor are there any conditions in a sale, nor is it permissible to sell what you do not have.”"
"5990","Othman bin Abdullah told us, he said: Saeed bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Al-Awwam, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Abu Hopefully, Othman, who is Muhammad bin Saif, said, on the authority of Matar al-Warraq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A man does not have to sell what he does not own.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5991","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, he said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: O Messenger of God, a man comes to me and asks me if I do not have a sale, I sell it to him, then I buy it for him. From the market? He said: “Do not sell what you do not have.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5992","On the authority of Ishaq bin Mansour, on the authority of An-Nadr bin Shumail, and Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, both of them, on the authority of Hisham al-Distawai, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Yusuf Ibn Mahik. On the authority of Ishaq bin Mansour, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Musa, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ya’la bin Hakim, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik, On the authority of Abdullah ibn Asmah, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, I buy goods, what is permissible for me, and what is forbidden. Ali? He said to me: “If you sell something, do not sell it until you receive it.”"
"5993","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi al-Mujalid, he said: I asked Ibn Abi He fulfilled the authority of the predecessors. He said, “We used to advance during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar, in wheat and barley. And dates, to a people, I don’t know whether they have them or not.” Ibn Abza said something similar, meaning that."
"5994","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Mujalid told us, he once said: Abdullah, and he once said: Muhammad. He said: Abu Burdah and Abdullah bin Shaddad competed in peace, so they sent me to Ibn Abi Awfa. So I asked him, and he said: “We used to say hello at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and at the time of Abu Bakr, and at the time of Omar, in righteousness. And barley, and raisins, and dates, to a people among whom we do not see them.” I asked Ibn Abza, and he said something like that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5995","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, He said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, and they were offering dates for two or three years, so he forbade them. And he said: “Whoever advances in advance, let him advance in a specified amount and weight, for a specified period.”"
"5996","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, borrowed money from a man, a virgin, and the man came to him to receive payment from his firstborn, and he said to a man: “Go. So he bought a firstborn for himself, and he came to him and said: I have only had a four-legged, best-born firstborn. He said: Give it to him, for he is the best of Muslims, the one who bestows justice."
"5997","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man had a camel tooth on the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came to pay for it, and he said: “Give it to him, but they found nothing but a tooth above Sunnah. He said: Give it to him. He said: You have repaid me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the best of you is the one who bestows justice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5998","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, he said: I heard Saeed Ibn Hani’, saying: I heard Irbad Ibn Sariyah saying: I sold a virgin from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I came to him to pay for it, and he said: “Yes.” I will not give you a judge for her except a Lujayniyah. So he appointed for me, and I did well, and a Bedouin came to him to pay him his age. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “Give him a tooth, and on that day they will give him a camel.” He said: “This is better than my tooth.” He said: “The best of you in judgment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5999","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, Yazid bin Zurayi, and Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, they said: Saeed told us. And Ahmad bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Ibn Abu Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade selling an animal for another.” Badly"
"6000","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “A servant came and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. upon him and grant him peace upon the migration, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not feel that he was a slave, so his master came and wanted him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He sold it with his own eyes, so he bought it for two black slaves, then he did not pledge allegiance to anyone yet, until he asked him: Who is this slave?” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6001","Yahya bin Hakim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The advance during the pregnancy is usury.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6002","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said, “He forbade the sale of habala.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6003","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayyub told us, and Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of pregnant women’s rope.”"
"6004","Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of pregnant women’s rope.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6005","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of a pregnant woman’s rope, and it was a sale The people of pre-Islamic times would sell to him. A man would buy camels until the she-camel produced, then she would produce what was in her belly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6006","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade \Sale of years\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6007","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Humaid al-Araj, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, “prohibited the sale of years”"
"6008","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Amara bin Abi Hafsa told us, he said: Ikrimah told us, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was wearing two burdocks of earth, so when he sat, he would sweat in them, as they became heavy on him, and he would move forward. So-and-so Jew has a garment made of wool, so I said: What if I sent for him and bought two garments from him to the best of my ability? So he sent for him and said: I know what Muhammad wants. He only wants to take my money, or take them with them. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He, peace and blessings be upon him: “He lied. He knew that I was the one who feared God and was faithful to them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6009","Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace, “He forbade the advance and the sale, and made two conditions in the sale, and profit unless he was guaranteed.”"
"6010","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayyub told us, he said: Amr bin Shuaib told us, he said: My father told me On the authority of his father, until he mentioned Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Payment and sale are not permissible, and there are no two conditions in a sale.” “And there is no profit unless he is guaranteed.”"
"6011","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the advance and sale, and two conditions in one sale, and the sale of what you do not have. And about making a profit that is not guaranteed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6012","Amr bin Ali, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, they said: Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, He said: Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two transactions in one transaction.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6013","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade muqāḍālāt, muḍābānah, muḍābānah, communicating with one another, and the two of them, unless \You learn\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6014","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, and Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ibn Aliyah, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the quarreling. And the muzabanah, and the mukhabara, and the mu'awamah, and the thaniyah, and he made concessions in the nakedness.”"
"6015","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Either “A person who harvests a palm tree, then sells its root, so the fruit of the palm tree is for the one who harvested it, unless the buyer stipulates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6016","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever buys a palm tree after it has been pollinated, then its fruit is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, and whoever sells a slave and has money, Then his money goes to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6017","Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: Sa`dan bin Yahya informed us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and my camel became tired, so I wanted to let it go. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed me and called. He struck him, and he walked at a pace he had never walked before. He said: “Sell him for a small ounce.” I said: “No.” He said: “Sell him for a shilling,” and I made an exception. We carried him to the city, and when we reached the city, I brought him the camel and paid its price, then I returned, and he sent for me and said: Do you see me? I only harassed you to take your camel and your dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6018","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Issa bin al-Tabbaa told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Mughirah, On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I marched with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, against a clearing of ours, and he mentioned words that meant it, so the camel crawled, Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rebuked him, so he spread out until he was in front of the army. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Jabir, I only see your camel.” It opened. I said: Your blessings, O Messenger of God. He said: Sell it, and you have its back until it comes forward. So I sold it, and I had a need for it. Severe, but I was ashamed of him, so when we had completed our attacks and approached, I asked him for permission to hasten, and I said: O Messenger of God, I am a newcomer. At a wedding. He said: Did you get married sooner? Or a married man? I said: Rather, a married man, O Messenger of God. Abdullah bin Amr was injured on the day he was injured. He left my maidens as virgins, and I hated to have the like of them, so I married a girl to teach them and discipline them. So he gave me permission and said to me: Come. He brought my family to dinner, so when I came, I told my uncle about selling the camel, but he blamed me. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, I went to him with the camel. So he gave me the price of the camel, the camel, and my share with the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6019","Muhammad bin Al-Alaa Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd God, he said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and I was on a camel. He said: “What do you have to do with the last of the people?” I said: My camel is tired. He said: So he took notice of his sin, then rebuked him, and if I were just among the first of people, his head concerned me. When we approached the city, he said: What? So what did the camel do with its meaning? I said: O Messenger of God, no, but it is yours. He said: No, but with its meaning. I said: No, rather it is yours. He said: With its meaning. I took him while I was still riding him, and when we reached Medina, we would bring him. When I reached Medina, I brought him. He said to Bilal: O Bilal, Weigh for him an ounce, and add a qirat to it. I said: This is something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, added to me, but it did not leave me, so I put it in a bag, and it did not leave me. It remained with me until the people of the Levant came on the Day of Hurrah, and they took from us what they had taken.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6020","Muhammad bin Mansour al-Makki told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, overtook me. And peace be upon him, and I was on a yard for us, so I said: We still have a yard that is bad, how anxious, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Will you sell it, O Jabir?” I said: Rather, it is yours, O Messenger of God. He said: O God, forgive him. O God, have mercy on him. He said: I took it for such-and-such, and I lent you He went to Medina, and when I came to Medina, I prepared him and brought him to him. He said: O Bilal, give him his price. When I returned, He invited me, and I was afraid that he would return it to me, so he said: It is yours.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6021","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard my father, he said: Abu Nadra told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd God, he said: We were walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was on a watering can, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Will you sell it to me?” For such and such, and may God forgive you? I said: It is yours, O Prophet of God. He said: Will you sell it to me for such and such, and may God forgive you? I said: Yes, it is yours. Abu Nadrah said: It was a word that Muslims said: Do such-and-such, and God will forgive you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6022","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I bought Barira, and its people stipulated that she be loyal, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Free her, for loyalty belongs to the one who gives The paper, she said: So I freed her, she said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, summoned her and gave her a choice of her husband, so she chose herself. And her husband was free.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6023","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, he said: I heard Al-Qasim, narrating on the authority of Aisha, that she wanted to buy Bureerah for emancipation, and that they had stipulated her loyalty, so she mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Buy her and free her, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees her.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with meat, and they said: This is to be given in charity to Bareerah, and he said: “It is charity for her, and for us a gift.” And she was given a choice (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6024","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that Aisha wanted to buy a slave girl. You emancipated her, and her people said: We sell her to you on the condition that the loyalty is ours. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Do not prevent you.” That is, loyalty is only to the one who is freed.”"
"6025","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim, who is Ibn Tahman, told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger forbade God, may God bless him and grant him peace, abstained from selling the spoils until they were divided, and from pregnant women being intimated until they put what is in their bellies, and from the flesh of any man with fangs. \of wild beasts\"""""
"6026","Amr bin Zurarah informed us, he said: Ismail informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, on the authority of Jabir, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The pre-emption in every trap, quarter or wall, is not right for him to sell until his partner gives permission. He sold it, so he has more right to it until he gives him permission.”"
"6027","Al-Haytham bin Marwan bin Al-Haytham bin Imran Al-Dimashqi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bakkar told us, he said: Yahya told us, and he is Ibn Hamza, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, that Al-Zuhri told him, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah, that his uncle told him that he was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bought a horse from a Bedouin, and he followed him to collect the price of his horse, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, hastened to He said hello, and the Bedouins slowed down, and men started attacking the Bedouins, calling him a horse, while they did not realize that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he bought it, until some of them increased the price more than what he had bought it for. Then the Bedouin called the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: If you I have bought this horse, otherwise I will sell it. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up when he heard his call and said: “Didn’t I buy him from you?!” He said: No. By God, I did not sell it to you. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I bought it from you. So the people began to seek refuge with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. As they were retreating, the Bedouin began to say: Bring a witness who will bear witness that I have sold him to you. Khuzaymah ibn Thabit said: I bear witness that you have sold him. I sold it. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Khuzaymah and said: To what do you bear witness? He said: With your truthfulness, O Messenger of God. He said: So he made it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the testimony of Khuzaymah with the testimony of two men.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6028","Muhammad bin Idris Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, he said: Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Abu Umays, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Al Ash’ath told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “If the two sellers disagree, and there is no evidence between them, then it is what the owner of the commodity says, or they leave it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6029","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan, Yusuf bin Saeed, and Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid told me, and the pronunciation is for Ibrahim. They said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ismail ibn Umayyah informed me, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Ubaid, he said: We brought Abu Ubaidah ibn Abdullah ibn Masoud, two men came to him and sold goods. This man said: I took it for such-and-such, and this man said: I sold it for such-and-such, so he said Abu Ubaidah: Ibn Masoud was brought about something like this, and he said: “I attended the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and something like this was brought, so he ordered The seller must take an oath, then choose the item to be purchased. If he wants, he can take it, and if he wants, he can leave it.”"
"6030","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bought food from a Jew for a small sum of money, so he gave him his armor as a mortgage."
"6031","Yusuf bin Hammad told us, he said: Sufyan bin Habib told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He died The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his armor was pledged to a Jew for thirty saa’s of barley for his family.”"
"6032","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: A man from Banu Adhrah emancipated a slave of his. Some time later, this reached the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Do you have any other wealth?” He said: No, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Who He bought it from me? So Nu`aym bin Abdullah Al-Adawi bought it for eight hundred dirhams, and he brought it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and paid it. To him, then he said: Start with yourself, and give alms on it, and if there is any left over, then to your family, and if any left over from your family, then to your relatives. If there is anything left over from your relatives, then like this, like this, and like this.” He says: “Before your hands, on your right, and on your left.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6033","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that a man from the Ansar He was called Abu Mathkur. He freed a slave of his who had died. He was called Ya’qub. He had no other property, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for him. He greeted him and said: “Who will buy it? Who will buy it?” So Nu’aym bin Abdullah bought it for eight hundred dirhams, so he gave it to him, and he said: Then If one of you is poor, let him start with himself, and if he is generous, then on his dependents, and if he is generous, then on his relatives, or he said: on his relatives. Have mercy on him, and if it is bounty, here it is, there it is.”"
"6034","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan and Ibn Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Ata’ On the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “sold the manager.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6035","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha told him, that Bareerah Aisha came to ask her for help in writing something, and Aisha said to her: Go back to your family, if they would like me to make up for it for you. Your writing, and your loyalty will be to me. I did so, and Bareerah mentioned that to her family, but they refused, and said: If she wishes to seek reward from you, So let her do so, and your loyalty will be ours. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Buy me and free me, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and said: What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions? It is not in the Book of God, so whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of God, it is not for him, even if he stipulates a hundred times, God’s condition is more deserving and more reliable.”"
"6036","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Men of knowledge, including Yunus, told me, And Al-Layth, that Ibn Shihab told them, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: Bareerah came to me and said: O Aisha. I wrote to my family for nine times, each year an time, so help me, and she did not complete any of her writing, so she said to her: Aisha, and she said to her: Go back to your family, if they would like me to give them all that, and your loyalty to me, then I did so, so I went. Bareerah went to her family, so she proposed that to them, but they refused, and said: If she wants to seek reward from you, let her do so, and it will be for us. So Aisha mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “That will not prevent you from her. Buy me and free me, for loyalty is only To the one who was freed, so she did so, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and thanked God, then said: As for what follows, what is the matter with people who stipulate conditions? It is not in the Book of God. Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of God, it is invalid. Even if there are a hundred conditions, God’s decree is more worthy, and God’s condition “Most trustworthy, loyalty is only to the one who frees.”"
"6037","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of loyalty and the gift of it.”"
"6038","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said, “He forbade the sale of loyalty and the gift of it.”"
"6039","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of loyalty and the gift of it.”"
"6040","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of water.”"
"6041","Qutayba bin Saeed and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, and the wording is his, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin A dinar, he said: I heard Abu Al-Minhal, saying: I heard Iyas bin Amr, and he once said: a slave, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He said: “It is forbidden to sell water,” and the wording is by Abdullah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6042","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Iyas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said, “He forbade the sale of surplus water.” He said: The ruler of the valley sold the water remaining in the valley. Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas hated him."
"6043","Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan informed us, from Hajjaj, who said: Ibn Jurayj said: 'Amr ibn Dinar informed me, that Abu al-Minhal informed him, that Iyas ibn 'Abd, a Companion of the Prophet (ﷺ), said: ""Do not sell surplus water; for the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade the sale of surplus water."""
"6044","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Wa’alah Al-Masri, that he asked Ibn Abbas about what is squeezed Of grapes, Ibn Abbas said: A man presented a narwhal of wine to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “ Did you know that God Almighty forbade it, and the word means “So a man walked to his side, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: With what? Did you please him? He said: I ordered him to sell it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who forbade drinking it has forbidden selling it. So he opened the two auctions until What was in them was gone (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6045","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha said: “When the verses of usury were revealed,” the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up on the pulpit, recited them to the people, then forbade trade. \In wine\"""""
"6046","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham. He heard Abu Masoud Uqba say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the price of a prostitute.” \the priest\"""""
"6047","Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, he said: Sa`id bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Mufaddal bin Fadalah told us, On the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Concerning things he forbade: And the price of the dog”"
"6048","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad informed us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir Al-Nasa’i said: This is an objectionable hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6049","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say in the year of the conquest, while he was in Mecca: “Indeed, God and His Messenger forbade the sale of wine. And carcasses, and pigs, and idols.” It was said: O Messenger of God, have you seen the fat of carcasses? Ships are painted with it, skins are anointed with it, and people use it in the morning sun? He said: “No, it is forbidden.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said at that: “God fought the Jews; for when God forbade them their fat They beautified it, then sold it and took its price.”"
"6050","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, that he heard Jabir, saying: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said about selling a camel’s horse, about selling water, and about selling land to be tilled. “A man sells his land and his water. Therefore, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6051","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, and Humayd bin Masada told us, He said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade \The stallion's honey\"""""
"6052","Isma bin Al-Fadl Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Humaid Al-Rawasi, he said: Hisham told us Ibn Urwah, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, who said: “A man from Banu Al-Saqq, one of Banu Kilab, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him about the honey of a stallion, but he forbade him from that, and said: We are honored for that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6053","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Na’am, he said: I heard Abu Kitten, he says: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the earnings of a cupper, the price of a dog, and the price of a stallion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6054","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun told me, he said: Muhammad told us, he is Al-Faryabi, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Abi Yes, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the honey of a stallion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6055","Wasil bin Abd al-Ala al-Kufi told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for the price of a dog and the price of a goat.” On the authority of Ali bin Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Amash, with"
"6056","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hazm, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Any person becomes bankrupt and then finds that he has the same commodity, he has more right to it than anyone else.”"
"6057","Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid and Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan told me, and the wording for it, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Abi Hussein told me that Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm told him that Omar bin Abdul Aziz told him, On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “On the authority of a man, he should be executed if he is found with him.” The item itself, and he recognized it, belonged to its owner who sold it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6058","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Al-Layth bin Saad and Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Iyadh bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, said: A man was injured during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the fruits of He bought it, and his debt increased, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give it in charity.” So they gave it in charity, but that did not amount to repayment. His religion, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take what you find, and you have nothing but that."
"6059","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, he said: he told me Usayd bin Hudayr bin Samak said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “decided that if he found it in the hands of the man who was not accused, then if he wanted He took it for what he bought it, and if he wished, he could follow his thief.” Abu Bakr and Omar ruled after him."
"6060","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Saeed bin Dhu’ayb told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: And he told me Ikrimah bin Khalid, that Usayd bin Zuhair Al-Ansari, then one of the Banu Haritha, told him that he was a worker on Al-Yamamah, and that Marwan wrote to him, that Muawiyah wrote to him: Any man who steals something from him has more right to it wherever he finds it, then he wrote With that, Marwan told me, so I wrote to Marwan: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “decided that if the one who bought it was one of the ones who stole it... He is not accused, so give her master a choice. If he wishes, he can take what was stolen from him for its price, or if he wishes, he can follow his thief.” Then he later ruled on that. Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman, so Marwan sent my letter to Muawiyah, and Muawiyah wrote to Marwan: You are neither you nor Usayd. You have two judges over me, but I judge what I have been appointed over you, so do what I commanded you to do. So Marwan sent a letter from Muawiyah to me, and I said: I will not judge. With it I was appointed, according to what Muawiyah said (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6061","Muhammad bin Dawud narrated to us, he said: Amr bin Aoun narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan On the authority of Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man has more right to his property if he finds it, and the sale follows the one who sold it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6062","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Messenger of God prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whichever woman is married to a guardian, it belongs to the first of them, and whoever sells something to two men, it belongs to the first.” \From both of them.\"" Qattan bin Ibrahim told me"
"6063","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, borrowed forty thousand from me, and money came to him, so he gave it to me and said: “Bless May God protect you from your family and wealth. The reward of the predecessors is only praise and recompense.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6064","Ali bin Juhr told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Al-Alaa, who is Ibn Abd al-Rahman, told us on the authority of Abu Kathir, the client of Muhammad bin Jahsh, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahsh, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he raised his head to the sky, then laid down his palm. On his forehead, then he said: “Glory be to God, what has been revealed of the severity?” We remained silent and separated, so when it was the next day, I asked him: O Messenger By God, what is this emphasis that was sent down? He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if a man were killed in the cause of God, then brought back to life, then killed, then... He was brought back to life, then killed, and he owed a debt. He will not enter Paradise until his debt is paid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6065","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Samaan bin Mushinj. On the authority of Samurah, he said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at a funeral, and he said: “Is any of the sons of so-and-so insulting us?” Three times, then a man stood up and said to him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: What prevented you from answering me the first two times, but I did not express anything good towards you. Indeed, so-and-so is a man? Among them, he died captive to his religion.” It was narrated by more than one person, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Samarra. It was also narrated on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as a mursal. We do not know of anyone who said in this hadith: on the authority of Simon, other than Saeed bin Masruq. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6066","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ziyad bin Amr bin Hind, on the authority of Imran bin Hudhayfah, He said: Maimouna was in debt, and she used to spend a lot of money, so her family told her about that, and they blamed her, and they found fault with her, so she said: I will not give up debt, and he I heard my friend and friend, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No one owes a debt and God knows that he wants to pay it off, but God pays it on his behalf in \the world\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6067","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, that Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took out debt, and it was said to her: O Mother of the Believers, You are in debt and you have no repayment? She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever takes a debt and wants to repay it, may God help him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6068","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “If one of you is followed by a leader, let him follow, and injustice is the aspiration of the rich.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6069","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Wabar ibn Abi Delilah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Maymun, on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who found it is mine, his honor and his punishment are permissible for me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6070","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Wabar bin Abi Delilah al-Taifi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Maymun told us. Ibn Masikah, and praised him well, on the authority of Amr Ibn Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “I have “The one who finds it makes his honor lawful, and his punishment is lawful.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6071","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, reading it, and I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The longing of the rich is unjust. And if one of you is followed by a group, let him follow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6072","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, said that a man from the Ansar was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to pray over him, and he said: “Indeed, Ali Is your friend in debt? Abu Qatada said: I will guarantee it. He said: With repayment. He said: With repayment? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6073","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Waki` told us, he said: Ali bin Saleh told me, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of you, the best of you in judgement.”"
"6074","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A man never did good, and he used to pay debts to people, and he would say to his Messenger: Take what pleases. And leave what is difficult, and go beyond, perhaps God Almighty will go beyond us. When he died, God said to him: Have you ever done good? He said: No, except that I had a boy, and I used to pay debtors to people, and when I sent him to be paid, I said to him: Take what is easy, and leave what is difficult, and he moved beyond, perhaps God He surpasses us. God Almighty said: We have exceeded you."
"6075","Hisham bin Ammar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Al-Zubaidi told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, that He heard Abu Hurairah say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There was a man who would lend money to people, and when he saw the insolvency of the insolvent, he would say: For his boy: He passed away from him; perhaps God Almighty would pass away from us, so he met God, and he passed away from him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6076","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Aliya, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ata’ bin Farukh, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God admitted into Paradise a man who was easy-going, a buyer, a seller, a judge, and a compulsive person.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6077","Amr bin Ali told me, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “Ammar, Saad, and I joined forces on the day of Badr, and Saad brought two captives, but Ammar and I did not bring anything.”"
"6078","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever frees a partner of his in a slave, he will complete what remains in his wealth, if he has wealth equal to the price of the slave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6079","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever frees a shareholder in a property, and has money equal to its price at fair value, then he will be freed from his money.”"
"6080","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Which of you If he has land or palm trees, he should not sell them until he presents them to his partner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6081","Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Idris informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, grants pre-emption in every polytheism that has not been divided, whether by quarter, or by a wall. It is not permissible for him to sell it until his partner gives permission. If he wants, he can take it, and if he wants, he can leave it. But if he sells and does not give permission, then he has more right to it.” On the authority of Yusuf bin Saeed, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, with (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6082","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, that Ibrahim bin Maysarah, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The neighbor has more right to his compensation.” On the authority of Mahmoud bin Ghailan, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, with"
"6083","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Husayn al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Amr Ibn Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, that a man said: O Messenger of God, there is no one in my land where there is no association or division, except the neighbors. So the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The neighbor has more right to reward him.”"
"6084","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Hamzah Al-Sukkari Muhammad bin Maimun, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The partner is an intercessor, and the pre-emption in every “Something.” On the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abu Mulaika, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6085","On the authority of Suleiman bin Dawud, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abd al-Aziz al-Majishun, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id and Abu Salamah, both of them, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “ruled by pre-emption in what was not divided, so if the limits have been fulfilled, then there is no pre-emption.”"
"6086","Hilal bin Bishr told us, he said: Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Pre-emption is in every property that has not been divided, so if the limits have been met and the roads are closed, then there is no pre-emption.”"
"6087","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz Al-Maruzi Ibn Abi Rizmah told us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided by pre-emption and generosity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6088","On the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman Al-Arzami, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The neighbor is more entitled to his neighbour’s pre-emption, and he is expected to do so, even if he is absent, if their path is the same.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6089","On the authority of Muhammad bin Hatim, on the authority of Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Shurayh al-Qadi said: Omar ordered me to “judge the neighbor by pre-emption.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6090","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told me, he said: Ishaq bin Issa told us, meaning the printer, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Awf, meaning Al-A'rabi, on the authority of Suleiman bin Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Learn the Qur’an, and teach it the people, and learn knowledge, and teach it to the people, and learn the religious duties, and teach them to the people, for I am a man under arrest, and knowledge will decrease, until... The two disagree about the obligatory prayer, and they do not find anyone to separate them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6091","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim Al-Khalal Al-Maruzi told us, he said: I am Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak. Suleiman bin Jabir said: Abdullah bin Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Learn the Qur’an and teach it to the people. And learn the religious duties, and teach them to the people, and learn knowledge, and teach them to the people, for I will be arrested, and knowledge will decrease, and temptations will appear, Until the two disagree about an obligatory prayer, they will not find anyone to separate them.”"
"6092","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal Al-Raqqi told me, he said: Muhammad bin Hatim told us, meaning he is Al-Jarjari, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar And Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ We will not be inherited, as long as we leave charity.” He said: And he said to Abd al-Rahman, Talha, Sa`d, and Ali: I appeal to you by God, you know that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “We do not inherit anything. We do not leave any charity”? They said: Yes (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6093","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar, and Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “We do not inherit anything, whatever we leave is charity,” meaning In that same way (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6094","Muhammad ibn Mansour al-Makki informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, He said: Omar said to Abd al-Rahman, Sa`d, Uthman, Talha, and al-Zubayr: I adjure you by God to whom the heavens and the earth are established. Did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “We, the prophets, do not inherit anything. Whatever we leave behind is charity”? They said: Oh God, yes (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6095","Amr ibn 'Ali Abu Hafs narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn 'Umar ibn al-Hakam, who is al-Zahrani, narrated to me, saying: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadithan, who said: 'Umar sent for me when the day had grown high. So I came to him and found him seated upon a bed, open at its side to its furnishings. When I entered upon him, he said: \O Malik"
"6096","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, they wanted to send Othman bin Affan to Abu Bakr. They were asking about their inheritance from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Aisha said to them: Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “No.” We are given an inheritance, and whatever we leave behind is charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6097","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Hajjaj al-Ahwal told us, he said: Salama bin Junada told us, On the authority of Sinan bin Salamah, that a man from among the emigrants gave in charity some land belonging to his mother, and she died, and she had no heir other than him, so he came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: My mother was one of the most beloved and dearest people to me, and I gave her in charity some great land of mine. So she died, and she has no heir other than me, so what do you order me to do with her? He said: “God has assigned you your reward and has given you back your land, so do with it as you wish.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6098","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, On the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbuh, who was shown the call, that he gave alms to his parents, then they died, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned it to him as an inheritance.”"
"6099","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Adhrami and Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam Al-Tarsusi told us, and the pronunciation for him, he said: Ishaq told us. Al-Azraq, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that a woman She came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I gave alms to my mother to a maid, and she died, so she returned to me for the inheritance, and he said: “He has rewarded you.” May God grant you the inheritance.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is a mistake, but the correct thing is Abdullah bin Buraidah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6100","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mukhurami informed us, saying: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, meaning Ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata’ On the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: A woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I I gave alms to my mother as a slave girl, and she died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God reward you, and restore your inheritance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6101","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna Abu Musa told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: I am Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I gave alms to my mother as a slave girl, and she died, and he said: “God has rewarded you and restored your inheritance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6102","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Basri told us, on the authority of Suwayd, who is the son of Amr Al-Kalbi, on the authority of Zuhair, who is the son of Muawiyah, And Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Husayn bin Ayyash Al-Bajdaidi told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ata told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that a woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I had given in charity to my mother. With a female child, and she died and left that child, so he said: “Your reward is due, and she returns to you in inheritance.”"
"6103","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Sa’id Al-Qattan, on the authority of Al-Ja’ad, meaning Ibn Aws, he said: You told me Aisha bint Saad, she said: Saad said: I complained in Mecca, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to visit me. I said: “Oh Messenger of God, I left money, and I only have one daughter. Should I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth, and leave a third to her? He said: No. I said: So should I bequeath? Half, so I leave half for her? He said: No, I said: So I bequeath a third, and leave two-thirds to her? He said: A third, and a third is a lot, three? Several times, he put his hand on my forehead and wiped my face, chest, and stomach. He said, “O God, heal Sa’ad and complete his migration,” and I continued to do so. I feel the coldness of his hand on my liver until now"
"6104","Amr bin Ali Al-Fallas told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, meaning Ibn Mahdi, he said: Sufyan told us, meaning the revolutionary, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, On the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit him while he was in Mecca, and he had only one daughter. He said: “O Messenger of God, should I bequeath all of my wealth?” He said: No. He said: The half? He said: No. He said: The third? He said: A third, and a third is a lot. It is better to leave your heirs rich than to leave them poor, begging people in their own hands.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6105","Musa bin Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi informed us, on the authority of Abu Usama, meaning Hammad bin Usama, on the authority of Hussein, meaning the teacher, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that a man gave land in alms to his son and returned it to him as an inheritance. He mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and he said to him: “Your reward is due, and your property is returned to you.”"
